From cb62dbc12a80b590be60fee4fc38322be647ee2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:04:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Characters: Wind Waker HD's actor light

Wind Waker HD lights characters with its own toon shader, read pixel for pixel from Cemu captures of Link and his
shield at Outset (10:00) and Windfall (21:00): the ramp as a lit/dark switch on the GameCube's lit channel, its
coordinate times the blurred sun shadow; the shade a hemisphere from actor C0 below to the palette's shadow colour
above; the lit side actor K0 times its factor (2.75 at noon); a rim from the view (pow(1 + N.V, 5), weighted to the
back-light, tinted by the hemisphere), all multiplied by the albedo in linear light and clipped before the gamma.

- gxc::toon_light_stage: the GameCube toon pattern this replaces (C0, K, ramp; then albedo x prev; optionally the
  effect-light stage PREV + K1 x ramp), and ShaderKey::hd_actor_light for matched draws with
  DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_HD=1 (off by default); other toon patterns keep the GameCube's shading.
- The effect-light stage (K1) is left out: HD drops it and sends K1 to its point lights, and its shaders have no
  such term.
- aurora_set_actor_light_hd(on, c0, shadow, k) from the host (linear); the light is used in the single-sampled
  scene pass at the frame buffer's size, with the shadow from the last frame's HD pre-pass.
- Matched draws mark the sea mask's alpha; the sun pass's shade, the HD rim and the exposure skip those pixels.
- DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_DEBUG (1 s, 2 shadow, 3 ramp, 4 hemisphere, 5 rim), DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_RIM,
  DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_LOG (each toon shader's TEV once).
- gxcore tests: the classifier, the flagged WGSL, and the formula against the traced HD pixels.

Characters: Wind Waker HD's actor light takes this frame's sun shadow

The characters' shadow came from the last frame's HD pre-pass, so on a moving camera or a moving Link its edge lagged
a frame behind the scenery's. Wind Waker HD draws its depth, then its shadow pre-pass, then the characters; this does
the same for scene passes with HD's actor light: the sea mask (with its own depth) is drawn before the scene pass,
a characters' pre-pass is built from that depth (the HD low pass, then HD's blur: 3 taps at 0 and +-1.36 texels;
mip 1 a quarter-size copy blurred and scaled back, as in HD's night capture) into g_actorLow, and the characters
sample its mip 1. The mask itself is unchanged for the passes that read it later. Other passes, MSAA and missing sun
maps keep the last frame's (DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_SAME_FRAME=0 for that everywhere, to compare).

From a save state at Outset's pier: against the last frame's shadow only Link and the King of Red Lions change
(6,049 of 1.2 M pixels); GPU busy 0.716 ms against 0.680 at 1680x720 (0.662 with the light off).
